# Normalise to LF in the repo, and check out LF for the files where the ending
# is load-bearing. Two of those here, both already burned once:
#
#   *.sh   — a CRLF shebang makes Linux look for "/bin/sh\r" and fail with a
#            bare "no such file or directory" that names the interpreter, not
#            the script. This breaks the container entrypoint.
#   *.cmd  — the opposite: with LF, cmd.exe eats the first character of every
#            line (`setlocal` -> `etlocal`) and still exits 0. See README.
* text=auto

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
